# E-ink calibration bench output. The contact sheets are regenerable and large; the JUDGEMENT is not
# — it costs a person standing at a panel for an hour and cannot be reproduced from the code.
# corpus.json is kept because labels.jsonl references images by path only: without the frozen corpus
# there is no record of WHICH 30 images were selected, in what order, or with what features.
bench-eink/*
!bench-eink/labels.jsonl
!bench-eink/corpus.json
!bench-eink/retest.jsonl
!bench-eink/drifttest.jsonl
!bench-eink/fullpanel_recipes.jsonl
!bench-eink/fullpanel.jsonl
!bench-eink/classes.json
!bench-eink/boxes.json
!bench-eink/ab_labels.jsonl
!bench-eink/wpfit.jsonl
!bench-eink/wp_predicted.json
# classes.json / boxes.json are DECISIONS, not output: a material class assigned by looking at 60
# works, and crop boxes authored one at a time on the panel. Neither is reproducible from the code,
# and both must reach the Pi by git — the harness reads them there. bench-eink/reference/ stays
# ignored because `eink_bench reference` regenerates it (and must, whenever framing changes).

# Local-only dev docs (kept on disk, not published).
# .ai/ is private-by-default; only the system architecture doc is tracked.
PRD.md
ROADMAP.md
CLAUDE.md
.ai/*
!.ai/system_architecture.md
